          "type": "intro",
          "title": "One Comment Can Undo a Whole Good Day",
          "content": "You got three compliments at work today. Then one coworker made an offhand remark, and that single sentence is the thing you are replaying at 11 p.m. The compliments evaporated. The comment stuck.\n\nIf that sounds familiar, Daniel Chidiac wrote this book for you. **Stop Letting Everything Affect You** (2025) opens with a simple claim: the cycle of **overthinking, overcaring, and overreacting** is not a character flaw. It is a **learned pattern**, and anything learned can be unlearned.\n\nChidiac's own line sums up the stakes: *\"In a world designed to keep you overwhelmed, learning to protect your peace isn't just important, it's essential.\"*\n\nThis first lesson covers Part 1 of the book: the root of why you absorb everything around you, and why it was never a defect.",
