          "explanation": "The book is clear that insight is necessary but not sufficient: knowing where the alarm came from does not switch it off. The habit has to be interrupted as it starts, which is what the later solution chapters teach. Option A is wrong because Chidiac frames reactivity as learned, not fixed. Option C is wrong because the book is self-help, written for readers to practice themselves. Option D has no basis in the book.",
