          "explanation": "Manufactured guilt is defined by the absence of a violated value and by its resolution condition: compliance, not repair. Option A is wrong because intensity is not diagnostic; real guilt can be intense too. Option C is wrong because real guilt (the forgotten birthday) also involves another person. Option D is a common context, but saying no to something that genuinely violated your values would produce real guilt.",
