          "explanation": "The reset ends in a decision per relationship: renegotiate if they showed up and there is something to rebuild, accept with limits if the relationship has value at the level they actually reciprocate, or release if the pause revealed only your own effort. Option A includes confrontation, which the reset specifically avoids. Option C keeps you in the over-explaining posture. Option D treats giving as the only variable, which misses that the reset measures what the other person does.",
